Relying on pragmatics is best when the semantics is sound, which is not cle=
ar here.=A0 I can't parse {nabyplane} off hand, so I'll skip that and also =
the awkwardness of having both {tu'a} and the elided predicate {citka} pres=
ent.=A0 The scope of {ma} is problematic: is it this world, where, admitted=
ly, the answer presumably lies, or the world of {lo nu do citka}, where the=
 language places it?=A0 Happily, the answer is a this-worldly {da}, which c=
overs the difference smoothly (the event world presumably in these cases in=
cludes the relevant portions of the actual world and, perhaps, then some).



